# Pruned from the initrd only, after common.list. Empty today: everything the
# initrd drops is also dropped from /usr and lives in common.list. The initrd
# keeps gpg, gpgv, gpg-agent and keyboxd to verify SHA256SUMS.gpg, and the
# wider GnuPG and lvm2 tool sets that /usr prunes in usr.list, because
# bluefin-server-boot.bst builds it from its own stack (initrd-stack.bst),
# whose lvm2 udev rules systemd-veritysetup needs.
